WEBVTT

﻿1

00:01:00.015 --> 00:01:03.265
Just packed up a real money load,
and it's coming your way.


00:01:03.352 --> 00:01:07.515
Look for "Rodgers" on the truck's side.
Don't forget my share of the deal.


00:03:57.527 --> 00:03:58.108
Shit!


00:04:39.445 --> 00:04:42.896
- Tuna on white, no crust, right?
- I don't know. How is it?


00:04:43.574 --> 00:04:47.868
Every day, for the last three weeks,
you've come here, asking how the tuna is.


00:04:47.953 --> 00:04:51.702
Now, it was crappy yesterday.
It was crappy the day before.


00:04:51.790 --> 00:04:54.578
And guess what? It hasn't changed.


00:04:55.211 --> 00:04:57.120
- I'll have the tuna.
- No crust?


00:04:57.213 --> 00:04:58.292
No crust.


00:05:22.530 --> 00:05:23.644
Thank you.


00:06:10.703 --> 00:06:13.076
Talk to me, Jesse.
This ain't working, brother.


00:06:13.164 --> 00:06:15.786
It's your fuel map. It's got a nasty hole.


00:06:16.209 --> 00:06:18.961
- That's why you're unloading in third.
- Told you.


00:06:19.045 --> 00:06:24.170
I lengthen the injector pulse a millisecond.
Just tune the NOS timer, you'll run nines.


00:06:32.017 --> 00:06:34.638
What's up with this fool?
Is he sandwich-crazy?


00:06:34.728 --> 00:06:39.354
- No. He ain't here for the food, dog.
- Chill out. He's slinging parts for Harry.


00:06:39.441 --> 00:06:42.940
- I know what he's slinging.
- He's trying to get in Mia's pants, dog.


00:06:43.028 --> 00:06:45.270
- What's up, guys?
- How you doing, Mia?


00:06:45.363 --> 00:06:47.522
- How you living, girl?
- Hey!


00:06:48.116 --> 00:06:50.524
Hey, Dom. You want something to drink?


00:07:01.546 --> 00:07:04.666
- He's beautiful.
- I like his haircut.


00:07:07.386 --> 00:07:08.417
Vince!


00:07:09.680 --> 00:07:11.672
- What?
- Can I get you anything?


00:07:13.433 --> 00:07:14.714
You look good.


00:07:18.897 --> 00:07:21.567
- Thanks a lot, Mia. See you tomorrow.
- Sure.


00:07:24.486 --> 00:07:26.443
- Tomorrow?
- I love this part.


00:07:31.201 --> 00:07:35.828
Try Fatburger from now on. Get yourself a
Double Cheese with fries for $2.95, faggot.


00:07:35.914 --> 00:07:39.414
- I like the tuna here.
- Bullshit. No one likes the tuna here.


00:07:39.501 --> 00:07:40.912
Yeah, well, I do.


00:07:53.432 --> 00:07:56.967
Jesus Christ, Dom! Would you get out
there? I'm sick of this shit.


00:07:57.061 --> 00:07:59.386
I'm not kidding, Dom. Get out there!


00:08:03.776 --> 00:08:06.267
- What did you put in that sandwich?
- That's funny.


00:08:06.362 --> 00:08:08.568
- Dom!
- All right.


00:08:27.091 --> 00:08:29.962
- Hey, man. He was in my face.
- I'm in your face.


00:08:31.596 --> 00:08:34.513
Relax! Don't push it! You embarrass me!


00:08:37.185 --> 00:08:38.465
Get over there!


00:08:39.979 --> 00:08:41.770
Jesse, give me the wallet.


00:08:44.650 --> 00:08:48.019
"Brian Earl Spilner."
Sounds like a serial killer name.


00:08:48.154 --> 00:08:49.945
- Is that what you are?
- No, man.


00:08:50.031 --> 00:08:51.988
Don't come around here again.


00:08:54.410 --> 00:08:56.319
Hey, man. This is bullshit.


00:08:57.372 --> 00:09:00.372
- You work for Harry, right?
- Yeah. I just started.


00:09:00.583 --> 00:09:02.125
You were just fired.


00:09:15.056 --> 00:09:18.176
Hey, Dominic.
I appreciate what you did, in a big way.


00:09:18.685 --> 00:09:20.179
Dominic, I owe you.


00:09:22.105 --> 00:09:26.648
Brian, you're messing with my business.
When Dominic drives, he's golden.


00:09:26.776 --> 00:09:31.403
Kids pour in. They want everything he has.
Every performance part. They pay cash!


00:09:31.948 --> 00:09:34.700
- What did Dominic say?
- You don't want to know.


00:09:35.035 --> 00:09:37.905
- What did Dominic say?
- He wants you out of here.


00:09:38.496 --> 00:09:40.454
- He wants me out of here?
- Yes.


00:09:40.540 --> 00:09:43.826
- And what did you say to Dom?
- What do you think I said?


00:09:44.127 --> 00:09:46.618
I told him, "Good help is hard to find."


00:09:49.799 --> 00:09:50.831
Relax.


00:09:54.513 --> 00:09:55.758
I need NOS.


00:09:56.306 --> 00:09:58.512
- I need NOS.
- No.


00:09:58.683 --> 00:10:01.471
My car topped out at 140 miles per hour,
this morning.


00:10:01.561 --> 00:10:05.974
Amateurs don't use nitrous oxide. I've
seen how you drive. You've a heavy foot.


00:10:06.775 --> 00:10:09.895
- You'll blow yourself to pieces.
- I need one of these.


00:10:10.153 --> 00:10:13.522
One of the big ones.
Actually, let's make it two.


00:10:14.032 --> 00:10:16.191
And, Harry, I need it by tonight.


00:11:27.982 --> 00:11:31.267
Hold up, hold up.
Look at this snowman right here, man.


00:11:35.614 --> 00:11:38.450
Sweet ride.
What you running under there, man?


00:11:41.203 --> 00:11:44.074
- Going to make me find out the hard way?
- Hell, yeah.


00:11:44.165 --> 00:11:47.035
You brave. You brave.
They call me Hector.


00:11:47.668 --> 00:11:50.456
I got a last name, too,
but I can't pronounce it.


00:11:50.546 --> 00:11:53.002
- Brian Spilner.
- Typical white-boy name.


00:11:53.341 --> 00:11:55.214
Know what I'm saying?


00:11:57.512 --> 00:12:02.387
See that over there? That's mine.
My baby. I ain't cutting her loose tonight.


00:12:02.683 --> 00:12:04.510
- Why not?
- I'm going legit, homey.


00:12:04.602 --> 00:12:07.271
Trying to get on the NIRA circuit.
Heard about that?


00:12:07.355 --> 00:12:10.356
- Hell, yeah.
- So, what's up with you, man?


00:12:10.566 --> 00:12:14.730
- I'm just waiting for Toretto.
- Shit. Better get in line. This yours?


00:12:15.905 --> 00:12:18.396
- I'm standing next to it.
- That's funny.


00:12:18.533 --> 00:12:21.202
You know,
Edwin happens to know a few things.


00:12:23.371 --> 00:12:25.577
And one of the things Edwin knows is:
It's not how you stand by your car...


00:12:25.999 --> 00:12:28.916
...it's how you race your car.
You better learn that.


00:12:34.883 --> 00:12:37.800
Oh, shit. Here they come. It's on.


00:12:53.193 --> 00:12:54.984
- Dom.
- Marvin.


00:12:56.696 --> 00:13:00.279
- Hey, Dom. How you doing?
- Hey, Camille. You been doing yoga?


00:13:04.663 --> 00:13:07.580
You did? Of course you did. Monica.


00:13:10.460 --> 00:13:12.453
I smell skanks.


00:13:13.171 --> 00:13:17.039
Why don't you girls pack it up,
before I leave tread marks on your face?


00:13:17.134 --> 00:13:18.047
Okay.


00:13:18.301 --> 00:13:20.971
- Letty, I was just talking.
- Yeah. Whatever.


00:13:21.388 --> 00:13:24.389
- Okay, Hector.
- Yeah? What's up, man?


00:13:26.101 --> 00:13:27.643
- Yo. What's up?
- Edwin.


00:13:27.728 --> 00:13:30.100
- How we doing this tonight?
- One race.


00:13:30.605 --> 00:13:34.734
$2,000 buy-in. Winner takes all.
Hector, you're going to hold the cash.


00:13:35.235 --> 00:13:38.236
- Why Hector?
- Too slow to make away with the money.


00:13:40.699 --> 00:13:43.368
- Okay. Good luck, guys.
- Hey, wait. Hold up.


00:13:43.869 --> 00:13:47.736
I don't have any cash.
But I do have the pink slip to my car.


00:13:48.207 --> 00:13:52.039
You just can't climb in the ring with Ali,
'cause you think you box.


00:13:52.252 --> 00:13:55.502
He knows I can box. Check it out.
It's like this.


00:13:56.507 --> 00:13:59.626
I lose, the winner takes my car.
Clean and clear.


00:14:00.052 --> 00:14:03.421
But if I win, I take the cash,
and I take the respect.


00:14:04.056 --> 00:14:05.087
Respect.


00:14:07.434 --> 00:14:09.806
To some people, that's more important.


00:14:11.939 --> 00:14:13.267
That your car?


00:14:17.069 --> 00:14:21.897
I see a cool air intake. It's got a NOS
fogger system and a T 4 turbo, Dominic.


00:14:22.074 --> 00:14:27.032
I see an AIC controller.
It has direct port nitrous injection.


00:14:27.288 --> 00:14:30.075
Yeah. And a stand-alone
fuel management system.


00:14:31.083 --> 00:14:33.159
Not a bad way to spend $10,000.


00:14:36.172 --> 00:14:37.630
You see that shit?


00:14:38.507 --> 00:14:41.793
He's got enough NOS in there
to blow himself up. Period.


00:14:42.720 --> 00:14:45.887
- So, what do you say? Am I worthy?
- We don't know yet.


00:14:46.599 --> 00:14:48.390
But you're in. Let's go.


00:14:49.268 --> 00:14:50.810
- All right.
- Let's go!


00:15:55.251 --> 00:15:59.083
- What the hell is going on around here?
- Street's closed, pizza boy.


00:15:59.589 --> 00:16:02.507
- Find another way home.
- Goddamn street racers.


00:16:03.259 --> 00:16:07.553
<i>Log on, 22. Code 3. Tension is high.
They've blocked the street.</i>


00:16:53.727 --> 00:16:55.102
Edwin.


00:16:56.647 --> 00:16:59.601
This is yours, whether you win or lose.


00:17:00.484 --> 00:17:03.105
But if you win, you get her, too.


00:17:12.621 --> 00:17:14.163
You're going to win.


00:17:15.541 --> 00:17:17.118
I'm going to win.


00:18:01.504 --> 00:18:04.374
<i>We had a reported homicide.
187, at Barabian Liquors.</i>


00:18:04.465 --> 00:18:08.842
I've got a 187 in Glendale.
Cops are all over it. We're good to roll.


00:18:09.554 --> 00:18:10.964
- All right.
- Let's race!


00:18:11.055 --> 00:18:12.086
Right.


00:18:21.858 --> 00:18:22.640
Go!


00:18:36.789 --> 00:18:37.904
Hell, yeah!


00:18:53.973 --> 00:18:55.598
Damn, that guy's fast.


00:19:03.775 --> 00:19:05.933
Let's go! Mčnage!


00:19:32.971 --> 00:19:35.758
No! Monica!


00:19:51.531 --> 00:19:52.990
Shut up!


00:20:47.713 --> 00:20:49.207
Well done, baby!


00:20:58.599 --> 00:21:00.508
Come on. Come on. Back up.


00:21:01.310 --> 00:21:04.644
Here's what you won, right here.
There you go.


00:21:04.730 --> 00:21:07.601
You were racing a bunch of skateboards.
Know what I mean?


00:21:09.026 --> 00:21:11.696
My sister holds the money. Count it.


00:21:14.740 --> 00:21:16.318
And you're my trophy.


00:21:19.579 --> 00:21:23.528
- Hey, Monica. What's up, baby?
- What's your problem? You didn't win.


00:21:26.502 --> 00:21:27.783
Fuck you then!


00:21:41.100 --> 00:21:42.381
Was that fun?


00:21:42.602 --> 00:21:44.511
Got a problem there, buddy?


00:21:51.235 --> 00:21:54.486
- What are you smiling about?
- Dude. I almost had you.


00:21:57.325 --> 00:21:59.116
You almost had me?


00:21:59.786 --> 00:22:02.241
You never had me.
You never had your car.


00:22:05.542 --> 00:22:08.708
Granny-shifting.
Not double-clutching, like you should.


00:22:09.629 --> 00:22:13.793
You're lucky that 100-shot of NOS
didn't blow the welds on the intake.


00:22:15.051 --> 00:22:19.429
- Almost had me?
- You tell him, Dominic. Get out of here.


00:22:20.807 --> 00:22:23.891
Now, me and the mad scientist
got to rip apart the block...


00:22:23.977 --> 00:22:26.550
...and replace the piston rings you fried.


00:22:34.321 --> 00:22:36.360
Ask any racer. Any real racer.


00:22:37.115 --> 00:22:41.576
It don't matter if you win by an inch
or a mile. Winning's winning.


00:22:41.870 --> 00:22:43.198
Yeah!


00:22:48.794 --> 00:22:51.878
<i>All available units,
we have street-racing along Hawthorne....</i>


00:22:51.963 --> 00:22:53.873
Oh, shit! We got cops. Cops!


00:22:54.174 --> 00:22:55.419
Go!


00:23:07.145 --> 00:23:08.937
Cops! Get in the car! Go!


00:24:33.191 --> 00:24:35.397
<i>Toretto, stop right there!</i>


00:24:37.111 --> 00:24:38.226
<i>Toretto!</i>


00:24:53.252 --> 00:24:54.451
Get in!


00:25:40.967 --> 00:25:44.301
You're the last person in the world
I expected to show up.


00:25:45.472 --> 00:25:49.386
I thought if I got in your good graces,
you might let me keep my car.


00:25:49.643 --> 00:25:52.976
You are in my good graces,
but you ain't keeping your car.


00:25:53.855 --> 00:25:56.856
You drive like you've done this before.
Are you a wheelman?


00:25:56.942 --> 00:25:59.314
- No.
- You boost cars?


00:26:01.738 --> 00:26:03.897
- No. Never.
- Ever done time?


00:26:04.282 --> 00:26:06.608
Couple of overnighters. No big deal.


00:26:07.369 --> 00:26:10.405
What about the two years
in juvie for boosting cars?


00:26:13.375 --> 00:26:14.869
Tucson, right?


00:26:15.585 --> 00:26:18.670
I had Jesse run a profile on you,
Brian Earl Spilner.


00:26:20.215 --> 00:26:23.382
He'll find anything on the Web.
Anything about anybody.


00:26:24.094 --> 00:26:25.505
So, why bullshit?


00:26:27.222 --> 00:26:28.716
So, what about you?


00:26:31.185 --> 00:26:32.679
Two years in Lompoc.


00:26:35.731 --> 00:26:37.522
I'll die before I go back.


00:26:43.655 --> 00:26:45.648
- Oh, great.
- What?


00:26:48.577 --> 00:26:50.949
It's going to be a long-ass night.
That's what.


00:26:55.251 --> 00:26:56.626
Follow us.


00:27:47.345 --> 00:27:51.556
I thought we had an agreement.
You stay away. I stay away.


00:27:52.975 --> 00:27:54.600
Everybody stays happy.


00:27:54.727 --> 00:27:57.052
We got lost.
What do you want me to tell you?


00:27:57.146 --> 00:28:00.064
- Who's "we"?
- My new mechanic.


00:28:00.441 --> 00:28:02.268
Brian, meet Johnny Tran.


00:28:02.402 --> 00:28:05.403
The guy in the snakeskin pants.
That's his cousin. Lance.


00:28:05.488 --> 00:28:09.189
So, when are you going to give me a shot
at that Honda 2000 of yours?


00:28:09.284 --> 00:28:11.691
- This your ride?
- It was. It's his now.


00:28:12.120 --> 00:28:14.611
No, it's not. I haven't taken delivery.


00:28:16.791 --> 00:28:20.492
Then, it's nobody's car.
But somebody put in the wrench time.


00:28:23.548 --> 00:28:27.166
- What do you think, Lance?
- It's an amazing machine.


00:28:27.844 --> 00:28:29.303
Yes, indeed.


00:28:31.514 --> 00:28:32.925
Let's go.


00:28:35.101 --> 00:28:39.514
I'll see you in the desert next month.
Be ready to have your ass handed to you.


00:28:39.773 --> 00:28:43.640
- You'll need more than that crotch rocket.
- I got something for you.


00:28:57.541 --> 00:29:01.075
- What the hell was that all about?
- Long story. I'll tell you later.


00:29:01.169 --> 00:29:02.794
Let's get out of here.


00:29:30.198 --> 00:29:31.313
NOS!


00:29:43.504 --> 00:29:46.920
- So, what the hell was that all about?
- It's a long story.


00:29:47.800 --> 00:29:49.709
Well, we got a 20-mile hike. Humor me.


00:29:50.719 --> 00:29:52.842
A business deal that went sour.


00:29:53.806 --> 00:29:56.890
Plus, I made the mistake
of sleeping with his sister.


00:30:23.085 --> 00:30:24.330
Take care.


00:30:29.425 --> 00:30:30.967
Yo, Spilner.


00:30:32.386 --> 00:30:34.593
- You want a beer?
- Yeah, sure.


00:30:35.264 --> 00:30:36.842
Oh, shit.


00:31:00.915 --> 00:31:03.869
We were all there, right? Falling behind.


00:31:03.960 --> 00:31:06.415
- With all that nitrous.
- Yeah.


00:31:13.302 --> 00:31:16.754
Yo, Dom. We were just about to go
looking for you, brother.


00:31:22.687 --> 00:31:23.967
Where were you?


00:31:24.063 --> 00:31:28.310
There were mass cops there. They came in
from every direction. It was orchestrated.


00:31:28.401 --> 00:31:30.773
- This your beer?
- Yeah, that's my beer.


00:31:33.865 --> 00:31:36.356
Yo, Einstein. Take it upstairs.


00:31:37.035 --> 00:31:39.573
You can't detail a car with the cover on.


00:31:40.413 --> 00:31:43.284
- Can't even get that right.
- You all right?


00:31:45.460 --> 00:31:48.331
- Am I all right?
- It was just a question.


00:31:52.092 --> 00:31:53.372
Yo, Dom.


00:31:53.635 --> 00:31:57.715
- Why did you bring the buster here?
- 'Cause he kept me out of handcuffs!


00:31:57.973 --> 00:32:01.805
He didn't just run back to the fort!
The buster brought me back.


00:32:07.691 --> 00:32:11.439
You can have any brew you want,
as long as it's a Corona.


00:32:12.112 --> 00:32:14.733
- Thanks, man.
- That's Vince's. So, enjoy it.


00:32:16.741 --> 00:32:17.986
You.


00:32:25.125 --> 00:32:29.205
- Hey, bro. You got a bathroom?
- Upstairs. First door on the right.


00:32:45.437 --> 00:32:48.853
He's got no call being up in here.
You don't know that fool for shit.


00:32:48.941 --> 00:32:52.440
- He's right, Dom.
- There was a time when I didn't know you.


00:32:52.611 --> 00:32:54.520
That was in the third grade!


00:32:57.741 --> 00:33:01.241
- Yeah. So, what girls are here?
- You name it. You want mine?


00:33:01.328 --> 00:33:03.736
- You need to shut the....
- You want two?


00:33:03.956 --> 00:33:06.625
- You don't have anything?
- You look a bit tired.


00:33:06.709 --> 00:33:09.496
I think you should go upstairs
and give me a massage.


00:33:09.586 --> 00:33:12.955
- Look at all our guests.
- How about you give me a massage?


00:33:16.302 --> 00:33:17.760
Crazy lady.


00:33:25.436 --> 00:33:28.105
You know you owe me
a 10-second car, right?


00:33:32.735 --> 00:33:34.015
Oh, shit.


00:33:39.784 --> 00:33:41.408
Did you wipe the seat?


00:33:44.663 --> 00:33:48.033
Jesus Christ! Would you cut this shit?
Come on!


00:33:50.130 --> 00:33:55.358
- Come on. Let's go get me a drink.
- We were just about to get along.


00:34:02.223 --> 00:34:05.390
- So, what do you want?
- Anything, as long as it's cold.


00:34:07.019 --> 00:34:10.602
You know, my brother likes you.
He usually doesn't like anybody.


00:34:10.690 --> 00:34:13.940
- He's a complicated guy.
- Yeah? What about you?


00:34:17.155 --> 00:34:19.480
- I'm simpler.
- You're a shitty liar.


00:34:21.200 --> 00:34:23.526
Well, I'll take that as a compliment.


00:34:25.204 --> 00:34:27.874
- But there's a problem.
- What's that?


00:34:27.957 --> 00:34:30.164
You need to get some sleep.


00:34:30.752 --> 00:34:34.701
And you definitely,
definitely need a shower.


00:34:35.673 --> 00:34:37.962
Come on. I'll take you home.


00:34:59.781 --> 00:35:02.698
<i>Show me your hands.
Very good. Now open the door.</i>


00:35:03.201 --> 00:35:06.321
<i>Put your hands on your head.
Behind your head.</i>


00:35:06.871 --> 00:35:10.454
<i>Face the front of the vehicle,
walk backwards towards the rear.</i>


00:35:10.667 --> 00:35:14.036
<i>Take two steps to your right.
Stop right there.</i>


00:35:17.090 --> 00:35:21.040
- What did I do?
- Shut up. He's clean, Sarge.


00:35:31.813 --> 00:35:34.139
Damn!
Muse, will you take these things off?


00:35:34.232 --> 00:35:37.150
- Shit. You put them on so tight.
- I like realism.


00:35:37.778 --> 00:35:40.103
You never know who's watching, Brian.


00:35:44.409 --> 00:35:48.193
Nice crib, Sergeant. It's a lot nicer
than the last place you confiscated.


00:35:48.288 --> 00:35:52.500
Ain't it? Eddie Fisher built this house
for Elizabeth Taylor in the '50s.


00:35:52.668 --> 00:35:55.585
You see, even the cops
are Hollywood in Hollywood.


00:35:59.341 --> 00:36:02.675
Okay, here he is,
fresh from Toretto's hot rod heaven.


00:36:02.761 --> 00:36:05.086
That was an $80,000 vehicle, Officer.


00:36:05.180 --> 00:36:07.387
- You told him what happened?
- He knows.


00:36:07.474 --> 00:36:11.389
- Send the bill to Johnny Tran.
- The kid's giving me attitude?


00:36:11.478 --> 00:36:14.230
It doesn't speak well
for police/FBI relations, Tanner.


00:36:14.314 --> 00:36:17.933
- I walk in the door and the guy's already--
- All right, all right.


00:36:18.027 --> 00:36:20.233
We'll talk, okay? Let's talk about it.


00:36:20.321 --> 00:36:23.606
Muse, why don't you make us
four iced cappuccinos, please?


00:36:23.699 --> 00:36:26.024
- Come on.
- Regular or decaf, Sarge?


00:36:27.620 --> 00:36:29.030
Decaf, I think.


00:36:29.371 --> 00:36:32.076
Four hijackings in two months,
and we have nothing.


00:36:32.166 --> 00:36:35.250
The DVD players and digital cameras
are worth $1.2 million...


00:36:35.336 --> 00:36:38.123
...which brings the grand total
to $6 million plus.


00:36:38.214 --> 00:36:41.049
We're in the political crosshairs now, Brian.


00:36:41.801 --> 00:36:43.627
That's why you're undercover.


00:36:43.719 --> 00:36:47.669
You want that detective badge fast, kid.
And you want to know something?


00:36:48.015 --> 00:36:50.850
The FBI can help,
if you come through for us.


00:36:51.894 --> 00:36:53.851
What does the truckdriver say?


00:36:53.938 --> 00:36:57.473
He gave us the same M.O.:
Three Honda Civics, precision driving...


00:36:57.566 --> 00:37:00.520
...the same green neon glow
from under the chassis.


00:37:00.611 --> 00:37:05.072
Lab says the skidmarks came back
the same: Mashamoto ZX tires.


00:37:05.157 --> 00:37:07.862
So, we know it's somebody
in the street-racing world.


00:37:07.952 --> 00:37:12.413
If we don't make this case, the truckers
will take matters into their own hands.


00:37:12.498 --> 00:37:14.206
I tell them we're close.


00:37:15.418 --> 00:37:17.327
Are you going to make me a liar?


00:37:17.420 --> 00:37:18.962
Look, what do we know?


00:37:19.046 --> 00:37:21.537
We know this world
revolves around Toretto, right?


00:37:21.632 --> 00:37:24.717
I'm not saying that he's the one
that's popping these trucks...


00:37:24.802 --> 00:37:29.132
...but I can guarantee he knows who is.
It's just a matter of time until I win--


00:37:29.223 --> 00:37:33.173
You want time, buy the magazine.
We don't have time.


00:37:34.979 --> 00:37:37.055
Just get me something I can use.


00:37:38.900 --> 00:37:40.560
Is Harry cooperating?


00:37:40.652 --> 00:37:44.234
Like a guy that'll do time
for receiving stolen property if he doesn't.


00:37:44.322 --> 00:37:46.445
What kind of vibe
is he getting from Toretto?


00:37:46.532 --> 00:37:49.652
He's scared of him,
but he doesn't think he's jacking trucks.


00:37:49.744 --> 00:37:52.116
- He's too controlled for that.
- Wait.


00:37:52.205 --> 00:37:55.325
Not that I want to contradict
Harry's fine judge of character...


00:37:55.416 --> 00:37:58.951
...but Toretto did hard time
for nearly beating a guy to death.


00:37:59.045 --> 00:38:02.165
He's got nitrous oxide in his blood
and a gas tank for a brain.


00:38:02.257 --> 00:38:04.166
Do not turn your back on him.


00:38:04.592 --> 00:38:06.135
Tanner, I'm gonna need another car.


00:38:11.683 --> 00:38:14.090
- What about parts and service?
- Hold off on it.


00:38:14.185 --> 00:38:16.511
Dom, I don't know what to do with it.


00:38:19.608 --> 00:38:23.440
All right, what the hell is this?
What do you got there?


00:38:25.196 --> 00:38:27.604
- This is your car.
- My car?


00:38:28.241 --> 00:38:31.195
I said a 10-second car, not a 10-minute car.


00:38:31.286 --> 00:38:35.118
You could push this across the finish line,
or tow it.


00:38:36.416 --> 00:38:39.334
You couldn't even tow that
across the finish line.


00:38:40.087 --> 00:38:41.285
No faith.


00:38:41.379 --> 00:38:43.787
I have faith in you,
but this isn't a junkyard.


00:38:43.882 --> 00:38:46.124
- This is a garage.
- Pop the hood.


00:38:46.426 --> 00:38:47.671
- Pop the hood?
- Pop the hood.


00:38:50.806 --> 00:38:54.471
- 2JZ engine. No shit.
- And what did I tell you?


00:38:54.559 --> 00:38:57.311
- I retract my previous statement.
- You know what?


00:38:57.396 --> 00:39:01.974
This will decimate all
after you put about $15,000 in it.


00:39:02.067 --> 00:39:05.816
Or more,
if we have to overnight parts from Japan.


00:39:06.280 --> 00:39:08.984
- We'll put it on my tab at Harry's.
- Yes!


00:39:09.408 --> 00:39:13.192
I gotta get you racing again
so I can make some money off your ass.


00:39:13.745 --> 00:39:16.450
There's a show down in the desert
called Race Wars.


00:39:16.540 --> 00:39:18.829
That's where you'll do it.


00:39:19.209 --> 00:39:22.543
When you're not working at Harry's,
you're working here.


00:39:22.796 --> 00:39:26.545
If you can't find the right tool
in this garage, Mr. Arizona...


00:39:27.885 --> 00:39:29.130
...you don't belong near a car.


00:39:32.723 --> 00:39:34.098
He owns you now.


00:40:01.419 --> 00:40:03.210
Tell me what you think about this.
Koni adjustables.


00:40:04.046 --> 00:40:06.253
Gonna save us about 2 pounds.


00:40:06.465 --> 00:40:09.799
And they're gonna give us
better traction for the hole shot.


00:40:09.885 --> 00:40:11.130
All right?


00:40:11.971 --> 00:40:14.047
This is your basic layout of the car.


00:40:14.140 --> 00:40:17.972
And that's pretty much
what it could look like when it's finished.


00:40:18.728 --> 00:40:20.103
Red, green.


00:40:20.730 --> 00:40:24.265
- You should be going to MIT or something.
- Yeah, right.


00:40:24.942 --> 00:40:27.777
No, I got that.... What's it called?


00:40:28.863 --> 00:40:31.021
That attention disorder--


00:40:31.115 --> 00:40:34.816
- ADD?
- Yes, that shit. Yeah.


00:40:35.953 --> 00:40:39.868
You know, I was good in algebra
and like math and shit.


00:40:40.708 --> 00:40:44.457
Everything else I failed.
Dropped out of school.


00:40:45.338 --> 00:40:48.458
I don't know.
It's just something about engines...


00:40:48.549 --> 00:40:51.669
...that calms me down, you know.


00:41:12.532 --> 00:41:14.988
- I'm outta here.
- Come on, dog.


00:41:15.618 --> 00:41:18.288
- Yo, Dom.
- Vince, get over here and give us a hand.


00:41:18.371 --> 00:41:21.289
Looks like you got
all the help you need, brother.


00:41:34.971 --> 00:41:38.091
- Mia! The chicken's dry.
- All right. I'm coming out already.


00:41:43.438 --> 00:41:44.932
Here you go.


00:41:46.858 --> 00:41:48.269
Hey, hold up.


00:41:48.777 --> 00:41:54.020
Because you were the first to reach in
to get the chicken, you say grace.


00:42:00.038 --> 00:42:02.743
- Dear heavenly....
- Spirit.


00:42:04.418 --> 00:42:06.078
Spirit. Thank you.


00:42:06.628 --> 00:42:11.836
Thank you for providing us
with a direct port nitrous injection...


00:42:12.801 --> 00:42:16.633
...four core intercoolers
and ball-bearing turbos...


00:42:16.805 --> 00:42:19.296
...and titanium valve springs.


00:42:20.058 --> 00:42:21.683
- Thank you.
- Amen.


00:42:22.811 --> 00:42:24.768
- Not bad.
- Amen.


00:42:24.855 --> 00:42:27.097
He was praying to the car gods, man.


00:42:28.442 --> 00:42:29.984
He's not the best.


00:42:30.068 --> 00:42:32.227
- What do you want?
- Practice.


00:42:32.321 --> 00:42:33.649
Thank you, girl.


00:42:33.739 --> 00:42:37.322
Look who it is. "Old Coyotes 'R' Us."


00:42:37.409 --> 00:42:40.161
I thought you weren't hungry, pumpkin.


00:42:40.329 --> 00:42:43.283
- You know, I gotta eat.
- He's always hungry.


00:42:43.374 --> 00:42:45.413
All right, sit down.


00:42:52.800 --> 00:42:54.709
How you doing, Mia?


00:42:57.888 --> 00:42:59.513
Here you go.


00:43:05.980 --> 00:43:08.731
- Jesse, hand me that chicken.
- Let's eat some grub, man.


00:43:08.816 --> 00:43:11.936
- Want some of that chicken?
- What, you rent a movie or something?


00:43:19.035 --> 00:43:20.944
Need a hand with anything else?


00:43:21.037 --> 00:43:24.488
No, I'm good. You can go join the boys
and watch the movie.


00:43:24.999 --> 00:43:28.664
- The cook doesn't clean where I come from.
- I'd like to go there.


00:43:33.841 --> 00:43:38.053
- I think we should go out sometime.
- No, I don't date my brother's friends.


00:43:38.763 --> 00:43:40.257
That sucks.


00:43:40.348 --> 00:43:43.681
- I'll have to kick his ass then.
- I'd love to see that one.


00:43:43.768 --> 00:43:47.053
I would pay to see that one, actually.


00:44:00.994 --> 00:44:02.702
Wash my car when you get done.


00:44:02.787 --> 00:44:06.452
- What was that?
- No, Mia. I'm talking to the punk.


00:44:07.292 --> 00:44:09.747
Wear your favorite dress,
'cause when you're done...


00:44:09.836 --> 00:44:13.121
...I'm putting you on the street
where you belong, cutie.


00:44:16.426 --> 00:44:20.126
Is this thing broken?
What's wrong with this thing?


00:44:21.389 --> 00:44:25.387
What was that Cuban restaurant
you wanted to take me to?


00:44:25.560 --> 00:44:27.553
The one with the picadillo and--


00:44:27.645 --> 00:44:31.429
- With red candles, wooden tables--
- The plantain, food all over the place.


00:44:31.524 --> 00:44:33.398
- What it's called?
- Cha Cha Cha.


00:44:33.485 --> 00:44:35.442
- Yeah, that's it.
- Yeah.


00:44:36.613 --> 00:44:38.605
Well, you can take me there.


00:44:38.740 --> 00:44:41.361
Friday night at 10:00. Is that good for you?


00:44:41.993 --> 00:44:44.033
- Yeah, it's perfect.
- Good.


00:44:50.460 --> 00:44:54.374
- There's no popcorn.
- Make your own goddamn popcorn!


00:45:08.395 --> 00:45:10.968
All right. Now that's valet parking.


00:45:14.901 --> 00:45:17.190
- Harry. What's up, dog?
- Nice to see you.


00:45:17.279 --> 00:45:19.106
Excellent. Come on in, man.


00:45:19.197 --> 00:45:22.317
- Check it. It's yours.
- Damn. What do we got here?


00:45:23.452 --> 00:45:25.943
- Hired some new help?
- Don't even think about it.


00:45:26.038 --> 00:45:28.493
- What's up?
- What's up, Brian? How you feeling?


00:45:28.582 --> 00:45:31.499
- Pretty good. What do you need?
- What's up, man?


00:45:31.585 --> 00:45:35.120
I need you to hook me up.
Three of everything. I made a list.


00:45:36.757 --> 00:45:38.714
Why don't you look that over?


00:45:39.009 --> 00:45:42.176
- When do you need this stuff by?
- Tomorrow, today, now.


00:45:42.596 --> 00:45:44.838
- Right.
- White boys work fast, don't they?


00:45:48.102 --> 00:45:49.430
That's right.


00:45:52.314 --> 00:45:55.814
- You said you need three of each?
- Yeah, three of everything.


00:45:56.610 --> 00:45:59.280
What do you think about that?
Check this out.


00:48:07.409 --> 00:48:08.951
He moans like a cop.


00:48:18.253 --> 00:48:22.417
Brian, this is one of those times
you need to be clear about what you say.


00:48:23.175 --> 00:48:25.167
Nod if you understand me.


00:48:25.260 --> 00:48:26.541
Nod!


00:48:28.388 --> 00:48:29.799
Sit up.


00:48:36.063 --> 00:48:38.732
Tell me what the hell you're doing
down here.


00:48:39.024 --> 00:48:41.480
Shit. What I'm doing?


00:48:44.071 --> 00:48:45.446
Dom.


00:48:47.699 --> 00:48:50.404
I owe you a 10-second car.


00:48:51.370 --> 00:48:54.988
And what this is about,
this is about Race Wars.


00:48:58.168 --> 00:49:02.036
I just went in there,
and Hector is gonna be running...


00:49:02.506 --> 00:49:05.044
...three Honda Civics with Spoon engines.


00:49:05.175 --> 00:49:08.011
And on top of that,
he just came into Harry's...


00:49:08.095 --> 00:49:12.342
...and he ordered three T66 turbos,
with NOS...


00:49:13.976 --> 00:49:16.052
...and a MoTeC system exhaust.


00:49:19.565 --> 00:49:21.273
So, what are you saying?


00:49:22.485 --> 00:49:27.028
You're gonna check everybody's shit out,
one garage after another?


00:49:29.909 --> 00:49:31.367
Yeah.


00:49:34.205 --> 00:49:38.119
Because, Dom, you know I can't lose again.


00:49:40.127 --> 00:49:41.503
He's a cop.


00:49:43.839 --> 00:49:44.954
He's a cop!


00:49:48.261 --> 00:49:49.589
You a cop?


00:49:56.102 --> 00:49:57.929
Let's go for a little ride.


00:50:00.940 --> 00:50:02.315
Walk!


00:50:21.711 --> 00:50:23.419
Okay. You stand watch.


00:50:54.160 --> 00:50:55.820
Yo, Dominic.


00:50:57.580 --> 00:50:59.240
There's no engines.


00:51:00.375 --> 00:51:03.127
What are they planning on racing with,
hopes and dreams?


00:51:03.211 --> 00:51:05.619
I don't know, but they're sneaky as shit...


00:51:05.714 --> 00:51:08.549
...and they've got enough money
to buy anything.


00:51:13.722 --> 00:51:14.671
What?


00:51:23.815 --> 00:51:25.144
We got a wolf pack.


00:51:25.650 --> 00:51:29.316
<i>It's Johnny Tran,
and he's coming your way really fast.</i>


00:51:29.780 --> 00:51:32.401
All right, we got company. Spilner.


00:51:58.392 --> 00:52:00.681
Come on. Move!


00:52:00.936 --> 00:52:02.976
Let me ask you a question, Ted.


00:52:04.481 --> 00:52:07.685
- Do you see anything wrong here?
- No.


00:52:11.572 --> 00:52:13.979
- We got no engines, do we?
- No.


00:52:14.074 --> 00:52:15.355
- Do we?
- No.


00:52:18.454 --> 00:52:21.027
A couple of Nissan SR20 motors
will pull a premium...


00:52:21.123 --> 00:52:24.159
- ... one week before Race Wars, huh?
- Yeah, probably.


00:52:24.543 --> 00:52:27.544
You're a smart fence, Ted.
Maybe too smart.


00:52:29.048 --> 00:52:30.957
What are you feeling, Lance?


00:52:32.468 --> 00:52:34.010
40-weight?


00:52:34.512 --> 00:52:36.338
50-weight?


00:52:36.972 --> 00:52:38.680
A 40-weight sounds nice.


00:52:54.282 --> 00:52:55.824
Where are they, Ted?


00:52:55.992 --> 00:52:57.818
- Where are they?
- Enough!


00:52:57.994 --> 00:53:00.485
- Where are they?
- They're in a warehouse.


00:53:01.038 --> 00:53:02.948
They're in a warehouse, man!


00:53:19.223 --> 00:53:20.504
Ted.


00:53:20.600 --> 00:53:22.260
Kiss my shoes?


00:53:34.530 --> 00:53:36.404
Let's go get our engines.


00:53:37.283 --> 00:53:40.070
My superiors are flying in from D.C.,
in two days.


00:53:40.161 --> 00:53:41.786
I want something to show.


00:53:41.871 --> 00:53:44.362
We've got a fence
with a lube hose in his mouth...


00:53:44.457 --> 00:53:48.075
...automatic weapons,
priors on every one of these Asian punks...


00:53:48.169 --> 00:53:51.503
...a garage full of DVD players
and generally psychotic behavior.


00:53:51.589 --> 00:53:54.958
Tell me why we shouldn't move
on Tran now and figure it out later?


00:53:55.051 --> 00:53:56.795
Because all we have is behavior.


00:53:56.886 --> 00:53:59.971
Let me get hard evidence,
because what we have now is just--


00:54:00.056 --> 00:54:02.049
What we have is probable cause.


00:54:02.142 --> 00:54:06.009
And truckers arming themselves for some
good old-fashioned vigilante mayhem.


00:54:06.104 --> 00:54:10.184
- Tell us about Hector, Brian.
- Latinos with spear guns. Give me a break.


00:54:10.442 --> 00:54:14.024
Hector's still working on the engines,
but the tires don't match.


00:54:14.112 --> 00:54:15.903
Will somebody give me a cigarette?


00:54:15.989 --> 00:54:18.112
- Get him a cigarette.
- Don't give him one.


00:54:18.366 --> 00:54:20.822
- I thought you quit.
- I did. Just give me one.


00:54:20.911 --> 00:54:22.654
- Get him a cigarette.
- No!


00:54:24.956 --> 00:54:26.581
Tell me about Toretto.


00:54:26.833 --> 00:54:29.620
I told you,
I think he's too controlled for this.


00:54:29.711 --> 00:54:34.338
Going suicidal on semi-trucks? No way.
Maybe Vince. But he's too dumb to do it.


00:54:34.716 --> 00:54:38.381
- I think the kid sister's blurring your vision.
- What did you say?


00:54:38.470 --> 00:54:42.053
I don't blame you.
I'd get off on her surveillance photos, too.


00:54:44.851 --> 00:54:46.096
Knock it off!


00:54:47.270 --> 00:54:49.808
What? Are you going native on me, Brian?


00:54:54.486 --> 00:54:56.728
Have you read Toretto's file lately?


00:54:56.989 --> 00:54:59.314
- Yeah. I memorized that file.
- Read it again.


00:54:59.408 --> 00:55:01.815
No, better still, take a look at these.


00:55:03.620 --> 00:55:06.989
Remember I told you about the guy
he nearly beat to death?


00:55:07.416 --> 00:55:10.701
Toretto did this
with a three-quarter-inch torque wrench.


00:55:11.211 --> 00:55:13.168
He's a model of self-control.


00:55:16.091 --> 00:55:17.799
I need a few more days.


00:55:20.554 --> 00:55:21.752
I need a few more days.


00:55:24.683 --> 00:55:26.261
Got a TR7 here,
with a ball-bearing upgrade.


00:55:27.645 --> 00:55:31.512
What it's going to do is,
it's going to spool up really quick.


00:55:31.690 --> 00:55:34.181
- I got this set up for 24 psi.
- Got it.


00:55:37.696 --> 00:55:39.488
You got big plans tonight?


00:55:41.617 --> 00:55:43.775
Yeah. We're going out to dinner.


00:55:45.371 --> 00:55:47.944
You break her heart, I'll break your neck.


00:55:48.582 --> 00:55:50.077
That's not gonna happen.


00:55:55.256 --> 00:55:57.083
I want to show you something.


00:56:11.355 --> 00:56:13.063
Me and my dad built her.


00:56:13.941 --> 00:56:16.313
Nine hundred horses of Detroit muscle.


00:56:17.612 --> 00:56:18.857
It's a beast.


00:56:19.447 --> 00:56:22.317
- You know what she ran in Palmdale?
- No. What?


00:56:22.492 --> 00:56:23.950
Nine seconds flat.


00:56:25.453 --> 00:56:27.576
- God.
- My dad was driving.


00:56:28.122 --> 00:56:32.334
So much torque,
the chassis twisted coming off the line.


00:56:33.419 --> 00:56:35.376
Barely kept her on the track.


00:56:36.130 --> 00:56:39.048
- So, what's your best time?
- I've never driven her.


00:56:39.133 --> 00:56:40.213
Why not?


00:56:42.971 --> 00:56:44.928
It scares the shit out of me.


00:56:47.350 --> 00:56:48.595
That's my dad.


00:56:50.103 --> 00:56:52.808
He was coming up
in the pro stock-car circuit.


00:56:53.231 --> 00:56:54.939
Last race of the season.


00:56:56.067 --> 00:57:00.279
A guy named Kenny Linder
came up from inside, in the final turn.


00:57:01.114 --> 00:57:04.613
He clipped his bumper
and put him into the wall at 120.


00:57:07.787 --> 00:57:10.159
I watched my dad burn to death.


00:57:12.709 --> 00:57:14.785
I remembered hearing him scream.


00:57:17.964 --> 00:57:22.507
But the people that were there
said he had died before the tanks blew.


00:57:28.892 --> 00:57:31.264
They said it was me who was screaming.


00:57:34.814 --> 00:57:37.222
I saw Linder about a week later.


00:57:38.610 --> 00:57:42.026
I had a wrench, and I hit him.


00:57:42.364 --> 00:57:47.073
And I didn't intend to keep hitting him,
but when I finished, I couldn't lift my arm.


00:57:52.457 --> 00:57:54.746
He's a janitor at a high school.


00:57:55.877 --> 00:57:58.415
He has to take the bus to work every day.


00:57:59.631 --> 00:58:02.336
And they banned me
from the tracks for life.


00:58:07.973 --> 00:58:10.464
I live my life a quarter-mile at a time.


00:58:12.311 --> 00:58:15.098
Nothing else matters.
Not the mortgage, not the store...


00:58:15.189 --> 00:58:17.680
...not my team and all their bullshit.


00:58:19.401 --> 00:58:21.773
For those 10 seconds or less...


00:58:23.280 --> 00:58:24.940
...I'm free.


00:58:45.427 --> 00:58:48.678
So, how is it, anyways,
that the gang came to be?


00:58:48.931 --> 00:58:50.046
- What?
- The gang.


00:58:50.140 --> 00:58:52.548
The gang?
No, they don't call themselves a gang.


00:58:52.643 --> 00:58:54.968
- What do they call themselves?
- They're a team.


00:58:55.062 --> 00:58:59.060
- They call themselves a team.
- All right. How did the team come to be?


00:58:59.525 --> 00:59:01.814
Well, that's a whole lot of history.


00:59:03.237 --> 00:59:06.938
- I've got time.
- Okay. Vince grew up with my brother.


00:59:07.908 --> 00:59:11.028
Actually, he didn't ever actually grow up,
as you can tell.


00:59:11.120 --> 00:59:13.113
But they were friends as kids.


00:59:13.331 --> 00:59:15.904
And Letty, she just lived down the street.


00:59:16.083 --> 00:59:19.333
Always into cars, though.
Ever since she was, like, 10 years old.


00:59:19.420 --> 00:59:23.003
So, naturally, you know,
my brother always had her attention.


00:59:23.674 --> 00:59:27.339
- And then she turned 16--
- And then she had Dom's attention.


00:59:27.637 --> 00:59:30.554
Yeah. It's funny how that works, isn't it?


00:59:31.307 --> 00:59:32.552
Yeah.


00:59:35.853 --> 00:59:38.344
How does Jesse fit into the whole thing?


00:59:38.481 --> 00:59:43.439
Jesse. Well, Jesse and Leon just sort of
showed up one night and never, ever left.


00:59:44.278 --> 00:59:47.564
It's just the way my brother is, you know.
Dom's like....


00:59:49.117 --> 00:59:51.074
He's like gravity.


00:59:52.203 --> 00:59:54.409
Everything just gets pulled to him.


00:59:56.040 --> 00:59:57.416
Even you.


00:59:59.627 --> 01:00:01.003
No.


01:00:01.129 --> 01:00:02.504
No.


01:00:02.964 --> 01:00:05.799
The only thing that pulled me in was you.


01:00:05.884 --> 01:00:08.719
Being friends with your brother
is just a bonus.


01:00:11.473 --> 01:00:13.015
That's good.


01:00:14.851 --> 01:00:18.386
That's good. It's nice to come first
every once in a while.


01:00:22.025 --> 01:00:23.056
Want to go for a drive?


01:01:01.773 --> 01:01:04.015
- Yeah?
<i>- The hijackers have hit again.</i>


01:01:04.109 --> 01:01:09.186
<i>Bilkins has decided that we're gonna move
on Johnny Tran and his guys at 17:00.</i>


01:01:09.281 --> 01:01:11.155
<i>Unless you say otherwise.</i>


01:01:11.241 --> 01:01:13.115
<i>If you agree, just say yes.</i>


01:01:13.744 --> 01:01:15.736
- Yeah.
- Who is that?


01:01:17.998 --> 01:01:19.741
It's just a wrong number.


01:04:11.965 --> 01:04:14.124
Yes, sir. Yeah, I know, but--


01:04:14.343 --> 01:04:17.012
Yeah. Yes, sir.


01:04:17.220 --> 01:04:18.631
Yeah. I got it.


01:04:23.018 --> 01:04:25.057
The DVD players were purchased legally.


01:04:25.145 --> 01:04:28.395
All we've got are a couple
of low-rent weapons charges...


01:04:28.482 --> 01:04:30.771
...and some outstanding speeding tickets.


01:04:30.859 --> 01:04:32.519
- So, they're out.
- Yeah.


01:04:32.736 --> 01:04:34.314
Father bailed them out.


01:04:35.447 --> 01:04:39.196
Is this the kind of intelligence
I can expect from you, O'Conner?


01:04:44.039 --> 01:04:47.206
- You're gonna put this on me?
- I can put it on whoever I want to.


01:04:47.292 --> 01:04:49.997
- Perks of the job.
- No, you can't put this on me--


01:04:50.087 --> 01:04:51.961
No, wait a minute. Let me tell you.


01:04:52.047 --> 01:04:56.259
I don't care if you have to aim at someone
and blow your cover to smithereens.


01:04:56.343 --> 01:04:58.881
You've got 36 hours to crack this bastard...


01:04:58.971 --> 01:05:02.055
...or you might want to think
about another career.


01:05:13.110 --> 01:05:16.526
It's Toretto, Brian.
It always has been Toretto.


01:05:17.907 --> 01:05:19.780
Tran and Hector are....


01:05:20.201 --> 01:05:21.992
They're just fumes.


01:05:25.247 --> 01:05:27.952
I know you've been lying to me.
My question is this:


01:05:28.042 --> 01:05:31.707
Have you been lying to yourself
because you can't see past Mia?


01:05:34.340 --> 01:05:36.333
He won't go back to prison.


01:05:37.301 --> 01:05:40.172
Well, that's a choice
he's going to have to make.


01:05:44.267 --> 01:05:46.674
There's all kinds of family, Brian.


01:05:48.104 --> 01:05:50.891
And that's a choice
you're gonna have to make.


01:06:08.916 --> 01:06:10.909
You ready for this?


01:06:37.320 --> 01:06:40.155
Nice car.
What's the retail on one of those?


01:06:40.782 --> 01:06:43.355
More than you can afford, pal. Ferrari.


01:06:49.541 --> 01:06:51.035
Smoke him.


01:07:45.973 --> 01:07:47.764
So, what's wrong, Brian?


01:07:48.725 --> 01:07:50.433
Nothing, man, I'm fine.


01:07:50.894 --> 01:07:54.144
Come on. Obviously something's off.


01:07:54.690 --> 01:07:58.390
Look, I have my good days and bad days
just like anybody else.


01:07:59.069 --> 01:08:02.652
Brian, don't lose that cool of yours.
That's your meal ticket.


01:08:04.616 --> 01:08:07.452
My meal ticket?
I can't pay for my own shrimp?


01:08:07.619 --> 01:08:09.078
I got the shrimp.


01:08:09.496 --> 01:08:12.070
No, that's one thing about me
you don't understand.


01:08:12.166 --> 01:08:15.831
I don't take handouts.
I earn my way, every step.


01:08:16.754 --> 01:08:19.126
I need something extra on the side,
like you.


01:08:19.215 --> 01:08:21.172
What do you mean, like me?


01:08:21.467 --> 01:08:24.337
- What's that supposed to mean?
- That's what I mean.


01:08:24.428 --> 01:08:27.133
- What does that mean, like me?
- Don't try--


01:08:27.431 --> 01:08:29.340
I'm not stupid, all right?


01:08:29.725 --> 01:08:33.805
I know that there's no way you paid
for all that shit you got under the hood--


01:08:33.896 --> 01:08:37.265
There's no way you paid for
what's under the hood of those cars...


01:08:37.358 --> 01:08:40.110
...by doing tune-ups and selling groceries.


01:08:40.945 --> 01:08:43.946
Whatever it is you're in on,
I want in on it, too.


01:09:06.804 --> 01:09:08.880
- Well, what is this?
- Read it.


01:09:09.682 --> 01:09:11.971
- What is this for?
- It's directions.


01:09:13.978 --> 01:09:15.686
To Race Wars.


01:09:16.189 --> 01:09:17.980
We'll see how you go.


01:09:18.983 --> 01:09:20.608
Then we'll talk.


01:10:06.906 --> 01:10:08.531
- How's it going?
- What's up?


01:10:08.617 --> 01:10:11.286
- Welcome to Race Wars.
- Great. Thanks a lot.


01:10:34.685 --> 01:10:36.392
Baby. Hey, baby.


01:10:37.562 --> 01:10:39.389
You should watch from the side.


01:10:39.481 --> 01:10:41.937
I wouldn't want to get exhaust
on that pretty face.


01:10:42.025 --> 01:10:46.105
- Put your money where your mouth is.
- I'll race you for that sweet little ass.


01:10:46.196 --> 01:10:48.652
You want ass,
why don't you hit Hollywood Boulevard?


01:10:48.740 --> 01:10:51.825
You want an adrenaline rush,
it'll be two large.


01:10:51.910 --> 01:10:54.911
Right here. Right now.
What's it gonna be?


01:10:57.583 --> 01:10:58.993
You got it.


01:11:19.021 --> 01:11:21.060
"Another one bites the dust"


01:11:24.360 --> 01:11:26.269
Come on. What you got?


01:11:26.987 --> 01:11:28.446
See ya.


01:12:04.442 --> 01:12:07.396
- What's up?
- Hey, what's up, Jesse?


01:12:07.862 --> 01:12:09.142
What's in your hand?


01:12:09.238 --> 01:12:11.610
Throwing down the pink slip, just like you.


01:12:11.699 --> 01:12:14.320
- The pink slip to what? The Jetta?
- Yeah.


01:12:14.744 --> 01:12:17.282
- You can't bet your dad's car.
- It's all right.


01:12:17.371 --> 01:12:18.652
I ain't losing.


01:12:18.748 --> 01:12:22.247
This fool is running a Honda 2000.
I'll win.


01:12:22.418 --> 01:12:26.961
That way, me and my dad can roll
when he gets out of prison. It's all good.


01:12:27.048 --> 01:12:30.666
They're gonna throw him right back
in prison after he kills you.


01:12:38.309 --> 01:12:40.266
You visualize the win.


01:12:40.353 --> 01:12:44.018
Visualize the win, Jesse. I'm serious.
You got to listen to me, man.


01:12:44.107 --> 01:12:45.649
Who are you racing?


01:12:50.029 --> 01:12:52.236
Jesse, don't do it.


01:12:52.365 --> 01:12:56.030
I bet you he's got more than $100,000
under the hood of that car.


01:13:19.184 --> 01:13:20.761
Too soon, junior.


01:13:24.397 --> 01:13:25.263
No!


01:13:28.401 --> 01:13:29.600
Shit!


01:13:30.237 --> 01:13:31.399
Oh, God!


01:13:41.832 --> 01:13:44.501
Yo! Heads up, bro. We got problems.


01:13:44.584 --> 01:13:46.328
- What?
- Jesse.


01:13:47.838 --> 01:13:49.877
Where's Jesse going?


01:13:50.048 --> 01:13:53.548
- He just raced Tran for slips.
- Oh, shit.


01:14:05.230 --> 01:14:08.350
- Where's he going?
- He went to the car wash.


01:14:08.567 --> 01:14:10.524
Whatever. Go fetch my car.


01:14:11.111 --> 01:14:12.736
Go fetch your car?


01:14:13.697 --> 01:14:15.357
We're not on your block.


01:14:15.449 --> 01:14:18.070
You better watch who you talk to like that.


01:14:18.619 --> 01:14:19.733
Toretto!


01:14:23.040 --> 01:14:24.914
SWAT came into my house...


01:14:25.876 --> 01:14:30.123
...disrespected my whole family,
because somebody narked me out.


01:14:30.839 --> 01:14:33.295
And you know what? It was you!


01:14:57.658 --> 01:14:59.698
Get off of him, man.


01:15:09.045 --> 01:15:10.836
Dom, chill out, man. Come on!


01:15:10.922 --> 01:15:12.713
I never narked on nobody!


01:15:12.840 --> 01:15:15.331
I never narked on nobody!


01:15:54.340 --> 01:15:55.420
Mia.


01:16:00.180 --> 01:16:02.552
I have respected you
and I haven't said shit.


01:16:02.640 --> 01:16:04.384
Now I am asking you not to go.


01:16:04.476 --> 01:16:07.346
- I'm doing this for both of us.
- Don't give me that crap.


01:16:07.437 --> 01:16:08.896
You're doing this for you.


01:16:08.980 --> 01:16:13.108
Why are you insisting on doing this?
Dom, please, just don't.


01:16:25.080 --> 01:16:27.571
- Mia, what's going on?
- What?


01:16:27.666 --> 01:16:30.157
- You know what I'm talking about.
- No, I don't.


01:16:30.252 --> 01:16:33.502
You always have tears in your eyes
when Dom drives away?


01:16:33.630 --> 01:16:35.172
What's the matter with you?


01:16:35.257 --> 01:16:37.830
What's he racing off
in the middle of the night for?


01:16:37.926 --> 01:16:41.093
- You know about the trucks?
- No, Brian! What trucks?


01:16:41.179 --> 01:16:45.047
- Jesus Christ. What?
- Listen to me.


01:16:46.309 --> 01:16:47.768
Mia, I'm a cop.


01:16:49.312 --> 01:16:51.982
What are you talking about, Brian?
What is this?


01:16:52.065 --> 01:16:55.517
Ever since the first time I met you,
I've been undercover.


01:16:56.778 --> 01:16:57.976
I'm a cop.


01:17:03.035 --> 01:17:04.659
Oh, you bastard.


01:17:07.497 --> 01:17:08.778
You bastard.


01:17:11.168 --> 01:17:12.995
- Mia.
- Get off of me, Brian!


01:17:13.086 --> 01:17:14.830
Mia! Listen to me!


01:17:16.089 --> 01:17:18.663
Everything I ever said
I felt about you was real.


01:17:18.759 --> 01:17:21.380
I swear to God.
You have to believe me, Mia.


01:17:21.470 --> 01:17:25.088
But this isn't about you and me.
Your brother's out there to pull a job.


01:17:25.182 --> 01:17:28.633
We're running out of time. Those truckers
aren't laying down anymore.


01:17:28.727 --> 01:17:32.476
Maybe they'll make it through tonight,
but every law enforcement agency...


01:17:32.564 --> 01:17:34.272
...is coming down on them.


01:17:34.358 --> 01:17:37.275
If you don't want anything to happen
to them...


01:17:37.361 --> 01:17:40.445
...you have to get in that car
with me right now and help me.


01:17:41.991 --> 01:17:45.324
Mia, you are the only person
that can help me right now.


01:17:46.120 --> 01:17:49.453
Please, Mia. Please help me.


01:18:01.385 --> 01:18:04.220
Civics are stashed somewhere
outside of Thermal.


01:18:04.305 --> 01:18:07.590
They wouldn't double back,
and Highway 10 is too well patrolled.


01:18:07.683 --> 01:18:10.637
- So, what does that leave us with?
- All this.


01:18:19.570 --> 01:18:22.441
<i>- Nextel.</i>
- This is Officer Brian O'Conner.


01:18:22.615 --> 01:18:26.992
Serial number 34762.
I need a cell phone trace.


01:18:27.203 --> 01:18:30.239
<i>- Okay. What's the cell number?</i>
- Mia, what is it?


01:18:32.375 --> 01:18:35.541
Come on, Mia.
She needs Dom's cell phone number now.


01:18:38.881 --> 01:18:43.590
323-555-6439.


01:18:44.679 --> 01:18:47.252
Thank you. Yeah, you get that?


01:19:13.458 --> 01:19:17.290
All right, we're one man short.
Letty, I need you on the left side.


01:19:19.589 --> 01:19:22.923
Your sister's right about this one.
This don't feel good.


01:19:23.051 --> 01:19:27.179
- Don't do that.
- Something's wrong.


01:19:27.263 --> 01:19:30.099
- Stop.
- We shouldn't be doing this without Jesse.


01:19:31.226 --> 01:19:34.180
This is the mother Iode.
We've been on this for three months.


01:19:34.270 --> 01:19:36.762
After this, it's a long vacation for everyone.


01:19:36.856 --> 01:19:38.814
- Let's go.
- I hope so.


01:19:42.362 --> 01:19:45.446
Listen, the other night I had a dream...


01:19:45.949 --> 01:19:48.654
...that you and I were
on the beach in Mexico.


01:19:49.035 --> 01:19:51.075
- Really?
- Really.


01:19:54.249 --> 01:19:56.407
Come on. Let's make this happen.


01:19:59.504 --> 01:20:04.000
- Leon, keep on those scanners.
- Copy that.


01:20:07.554 --> 01:20:09.594
All right, let's go.


01:20:20.192 --> 01:20:23.276
<i>Okay, we traced the number
to the northbound 86.</i>


01:20:23.362 --> 01:20:27.858
<i>Mile 114, outside Coachella.
We'll keep the trace open, Officer.</i>


01:20:28.200 --> 01:20:29.611
Let me see this.


01:20:34.414 --> 01:20:36.656
I think we're about 40 miles away.


01:20:37.084 --> 01:20:38.708
What are you gonna do?


01:20:40.003 --> 01:20:41.996
What are you gonna do?


01:21:14.288 --> 01:21:16.364
Okay! Go time!


01:21:32.056 --> 01:21:34.512
We're all good.
I got nothing on the scanners.


01:21:34.600 --> 01:21:35.881
Keep going.


01:21:50.450 --> 01:21:51.612
Vince!


01:21:52.285 --> 01:21:54.361
Vince, don't! Get back in!


01:21:55.955 --> 01:21:57.070
Vince!


01:22:02.712 --> 01:22:04.420
He's got a damn shotgun! Leon!


01:22:04.505 --> 01:22:06.794
Back off! Get him off of there!


01:22:09.469 --> 01:22:10.749
Oh, shit!


01:22:21.814 --> 01:22:24.484
Get me off this thing! Pull up!


01:22:25.610 --> 01:22:28.944
Unhook yourself. Do it!


01:22:29.322 --> 01:22:31.315
- Do it!
- I can't get--


01:22:31.408 --> 01:22:32.783
You can do it!


01:22:33.827 --> 01:22:35.285
Come on, Vince!


01:22:42.794 --> 01:22:45.367
Dom! I'm pulling up to distract him!


01:22:52.846 --> 01:22:54.305
Come on, boy!


01:22:55.515 --> 01:22:57.638
Shot doesn't get better than this.


01:23:02.689 --> 01:23:03.970
Son of a bitch!


01:23:08.820 --> 01:23:11.146
Take me off here,
or I'll have to unhook the wire!


01:23:11.239 --> 01:23:15.486
Try it again. One, two, three!


01:23:27.506 --> 01:23:29.083
Unhook yourself!


01:23:30.842 --> 01:23:32.716
I can't get my arm free!


01:23:32.803 --> 01:23:35.045
- Vince, grab my hand!
- My arm!


01:23:35.138 --> 01:23:36.930
Listen, give me your hand.


01:23:37.099 --> 01:23:39.554
I'm gonna pull you off the rig!


01:23:42.729 --> 01:23:44.354
Vince!


01:23:44.440 --> 01:23:46.432
Hold on!


01:23:46.525 --> 01:23:48.648
Give me your hand! Listen to me!


01:23:55.492 --> 01:23:56.488
Dominic!


01:23:56.577 --> 01:23:57.775
Shit!


01:24:01.332 --> 01:24:03.455
- Dominic!
- Hang on!


01:24:04.043 --> 01:24:06.960
Dom! Move out of the way.
I'm coming to get him.


01:24:32.071 --> 01:24:33.399
Letty!


01:24:34.198 --> 01:24:35.229
Leon!


01:24:35.324 --> 01:24:36.403
Pull back for Letty.


01:24:36.492 --> 01:24:37.772
<i>Get her out of there!</i>


01:24:37.868 --> 01:24:39.279
I'm on it! Go!


01:24:48.462 --> 01:24:51.132
I've got her! You get Vince off that truck.


01:24:56.471 --> 01:24:58.712
Letty! Come on, baby.


01:24:59.765 --> 01:25:00.845
You okay?


01:25:00.933 --> 01:25:03.341
Oh, shit. Come on, girl, you all right?


01:25:03.436 --> 01:25:07.019
Come on, let me look at you.
Come on. We got to go. Let's go.


01:25:20.828 --> 01:25:22.323
Vince!


01:25:50.608 --> 01:25:51.771
Take the wheel.


01:25:51.860 --> 01:25:54.565
- What do you mean?
- Put your foot on the gas!


01:25:55.322 --> 01:25:57.610
I'm gonna get him.
Put your foot on the gas!


01:25:57.699 --> 01:25:58.944
Okay!


01:26:02.329 --> 01:26:05.413
- Come on. Keep it steady.
- I got it!


01:26:06.958 --> 01:26:08.915
All right, hold on, Vince.


01:26:09.711 --> 01:26:12.629
He's having a hard time holding on.
Get me a little closer.


01:26:12.714 --> 01:26:13.995
All right.


01:26:14.841 --> 01:26:17.000
- Closer.
- I'm moving in.


01:26:17.385 --> 01:26:18.963
Hold it right there!


01:26:19.805 --> 01:26:20.884
Go!


01:26:23.058 --> 01:26:25.631
You got to hang in here with me now!


01:26:25.727 --> 01:26:27.886
We'll get you off. Give me your arm!


01:26:27.979 --> 01:26:30.138
Vince, look at me! Don't let go!


01:26:34.111 --> 01:26:36.684
Come on, Vince!
Throw this arm around me!


01:26:37.489 --> 01:26:39.814
Vince, don't let go!


01:26:44.037 --> 01:26:46.113
Come on, Mia. Get closer!


01:26:51.670 --> 01:26:53.378
Mia, get closer! Come on.


01:26:53.464 --> 01:26:55.337
Come on, Vince. Here we go!


01:27:23.410 --> 01:27:24.691
Shit.


01:27:28.332 --> 01:27:31.867
It's gonna be okay, Letty. I love you.


01:27:35.131 --> 01:27:36.755
- Watch her.
- I got her.


01:27:37.675 --> 01:27:40.213
Come on, Vince! Hang in there! Come on!


01:27:44.390 --> 01:27:47.557
If he doesn't get to an ambulance
in 10 minutes, he's dead.


01:27:47.643 --> 01:27:50.099
- Hold the pressure. Hold his arm up.
- I got it.


01:27:56.027 --> 01:27:58.981
Yeah. Yeah, this is Officer Brian O'Conner.


01:27:59.196 --> 01:28:01.652
I'm off-duty MAPD.


01:28:01.782 --> 01:28:04.570
I need a life flight roll out right away.


01:28:05.703 --> 01:28:09.997
My 20 is Highway 86, mile marker 147.


01:28:10.541 --> 01:28:13.578
I got one trauma victim,
about 24 years of age.


01:28:13.669 --> 01:28:16.243
Six-foot, maybe 200 pounds.


01:28:16.422 --> 01:28:20.171
He's got a deep laceration to his right arm
with arterial bleeding.


01:28:20.259 --> 01:28:24.637
And he's got a shotgun wound
close range to his left flank.


01:28:26.557 --> 01:28:28.467
Yeah, he's going into shock!


01:30:08.535 --> 01:30:10.445
Dom, put the gun down now!


01:30:13.040 --> 01:30:14.867
- Move your car.
- No bullshit!


01:30:14.958 --> 01:30:17.414
Put it down now! No more running!


01:30:17.544 --> 01:30:19.087
I'm not running!


01:30:22.216 --> 01:30:24.623
- Where's Leon and Letty?
- They're long gone!


01:30:24.718 --> 01:30:27.755
Then it's over.
I didn't call the police, but don't push me!


01:30:27.846 --> 01:30:30.764
- Put the gun down. I swear to God!
- You are the cop!


01:30:30.849 --> 01:30:32.260
You're a cop!


01:30:33.853 --> 01:30:37.222
Brian, I got to find Jesse before they do.


01:30:37.314 --> 01:30:40.185
- I'm all the kid's got.
- I'll call in the plates.


01:30:40.276 --> 01:30:43.976
PD will pick him up way before
Johnny even gets near him.


01:30:44.155 --> 01:30:47.606
- Move your car.
- Dom, stop it! It's over. Please.


01:30:47.742 --> 01:30:49.449
Mia, stay out of it!


01:30:54.999 --> 01:30:58.202
Dominic, I am so sorry.


01:30:58.586 --> 01:31:00.792
I don't know what I'm doing, Dom.


01:31:00.880 --> 01:31:05.127
I'm so scared right now.
I don't know what's going on.


01:31:05.217 --> 01:31:07.969
What were you thinking, man?


01:31:08.054 --> 01:31:10.545
I don't know! I panicked! I'm sorry.


01:31:10.640 --> 01:31:12.549
I'm scared!


01:31:12.642 --> 01:31:15.726
I don't know what I'm doing!
Will you please help me?


01:31:20.274 --> 01:31:21.769
Dom!


01:31:40.628 --> 01:31:41.957
Jesse!


01:31:42.046 --> 01:31:43.541
No, Jesse!


01:31:58.271 --> 01:31:59.896
No, Dom, no!


01:34:54.782 --> 01:34:58.151
Call 911. You call 911!


01:35:32.988 --> 01:35:35.739
I used to drag here back in high school.


01:35:36.449 --> 01:35:40.613
That railroad crossing up there
is exactly a quarter mile away from here.


01:35:41.788 --> 01:35:44.410
On green, I'm going for it.


01:38:18.988 --> 01:38:21.230
That's not what I had in mind.


01:39:07.788 --> 01:39:09.697
You know what you're doing?


01:39:10.165 --> 01:39:12.241
I owe you a 10-second car.

